{"chunk_id": "bf537f4d-f12b-47df-a911-a527ab750033", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 19, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 70, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P01\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter did not know how to write in a candidate and needed to be instructed by the poll worker.\n2. Later, the voter wanted to perform an additional write-in but had forgotten how and needed to be\nreminded by the poll worker.\n3. The voter required a poll worker to escort her to the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625742+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "f2ecfbfe-0eb7-48cd-bebf-1b10d1f3cb39", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 20, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 93, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P02\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter could not hear the initial audio instructions and was unfamiliar with the navigation keypad so\nshe required assistance from a poll worker in order to increase the volume.\n2. During the write-in session, the voter asked the poll worker where she could find the space key.\n3. The voter asked the poll worker how she could go back and change one of her votes.\n4. The voter required a poll worker to escort her to the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625749+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ba2863a7-bdd1-4c8c-9e1b-50587dfa29ea", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 21, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 41, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P03\nLow Vision | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter asked the poll worker if there was a button that would allow her to review her ballot at any\ntime during the voting process.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625754+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "6e4228f5-7dc6-4aa6-9996-d9a2346a64ce", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 22, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 113, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P04\nBlind,\nOver 65 | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter encountered a system error and could not continue. The poll worker reset the machine and\nbegan the voting session again.\n2. The voter did not know how to write in a candidate and needed to be instructed by the poll worker.\n3. During the write-in session, the voter had difficulty understanding the audio and was unable to tell if she\nhad spelled the name of her candidate correctly. She asked the poll worker to read aloud the letters that\nhad been entered.\n4. The voter required a poll worker to escort her to the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625761+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "64310108-e261-4767-abd3-06579adb6cbe", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 23, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 68, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P05\nMild Cognitive\nImpairment and\nLow Literacy | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter was unsure how to proceed after the ballot was printed. The poll worker instructed him to\ninsert the printed ballot into the scanner.\n2. After successfully inserting his marked ballot into the scanner/tabulator, the voter called a poll worker and\nasked what he had to do next.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625768+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b0d4fe41-1658-46e4-abfc-de9978466ed6", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 24, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 30, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P06\nLow Vision | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter needed confirmation from the poll worker as to whether he had successfully voted.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625772+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "cf3f9429-a8a7-46e9-82a7-ab5092fce098", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 25, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 74, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P07\nBlind and\nImpaired Mobility | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter required assistance from a poll worker in order to increase the volume of the audio instructions.\nHe could not hear the initial audio and wasn’t sure if it was too quiet or if he needed to press a button to\nstart it.\n2. The voter required a poll worker to escort him to the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625780+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "9c54523c-9eb1-44c4-8813-d6bb9a78eefa", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 26, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 92, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P08\nQuadriplegic | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter (who had requested audio despite using a touch screen) was confused by the audio since it was\ngiving him instructions that were only appropriate for the navigation keypad and not applicable to the\ntouch screen interface. The participant requested clarification of how he should proceed.\n2. Since the participant was unable to hold the ballot himself, he required a poll worker to take the ballot out\nof the ExpressVote machine and insert it into the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625787+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "46676606-7ca1-432e-8aec-152d4f0da7e5", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 27, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 99, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P09\nLow Vision,\nOver 65 | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The initial volume level was too low for the participant, so he couldn’t hear how to begin the voting\nsession. The poll worker helped him to adjust the audio level and got him started.\n2. The voter asked the poll worker again how he could make the volume louder.\n3. The voter asked the poll worker to restart his voting session so he could start again at the beginning.\n4. The voter asked how he should insert the ballot into the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625794+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b365a77b-7ea2-429f-83c3-cad0bcdca99a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 28, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 52, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P11\nMild Cognitive\nImpairment and\nLow Literacy | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter did not realize that the ballot scanner/tabulator also casts the ballot. She called a poll worker\nto ask if she was going to receive the ballot back after it was inserted.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625800+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "01e71599-57f6-4804-9cbe-525a11a75d82", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 29, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 31, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P12\nLow Vision | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter asked for instructions about where to submit his ballot once he had finished voting.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625804+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "275bcf77-a8bc-4d32-9c3c-879b729fd9fb", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 30, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 92, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P13\nImpaired Mobility\nand Dexterity | INTERFACE\nUSED: Paddle\nButtons | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter did not understand how to navigate the ballot with the paddle buttons. Specifically, he did not\nunderstand that the paddle buttons only cycle through the options which are currently visible on the\nscreen, instead of cycling through all available options. He wanted to know how he could scroll back up\nthrough the options. The poll worker told him to select the “more” option on screen in order to navigate\nthrough all available candidates.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625812+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "19b37899-d236-4806-b930-e1c8c3197944", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 31, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 39, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P14\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter needed an explanation of the keys on the Navigation Keypad.\n2. The voter required a poll worker to escort him to the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625817+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ef05a1d4-acf8-400e-beea-7c1e57b83034", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 32, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 91, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P15\nLow Vision and\nHearing Impairment | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter struggled with initially inserting the ballot into the ExpressVote machine and had to call a poll\nworker to help him insert the ballot at the correct angle.\n2. After the voter inserted the ballot into the scanner/tabulator, he was unsure if he was finished voting or\nif he should wait for the ballot to come back out. He required confirmation from a poll worker to ensure\nthat he had finished voting.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625824+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "5e541355-af87-43c1-9194-a199e22ba8d2", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 33, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 77, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P16\nLow Vision | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter was unsure how to go back and change her vote in a contest.\n2. Once at the scanner, the voter had to ask a poll worker how to insert the ballot into the machine.\n3. The voter fed the ballot into the incorrect slot and required assistance from a poll worker in order to\nsubmit it into the correct tray.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625830+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "632ea2ab-ca34-473e-8114-2b2765f435ea", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 34, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 83, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P17\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter did not know how to insert a space during her write-in vote.\n2. Once the participant had finished marking her ballot, she was unsure how to scan it for the vote to be\ncast. She called a poll worker, who escorted her to the scanner.\n3. Once the ballot was placed into the scanner, the voter was unsure whether she had successfully cast her\nvote or not.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625836+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b2109190-37c1-4e59-8c6b-dedf92e16f89", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 35, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 49, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P17\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Paddle\nButtons | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The participant accidentally hit the exit button, and was alerted that she could exit the voting session and\neject her ballot. She called a poll worker to assist her in returning to the voting session.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625841+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e577e627-4b30-45e7-ad33-9709a9753311", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 36, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 33, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P18\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter required a poll worker to escort him to the scanner and explain how to insert the ballot.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625846+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ee29bf19-bfd8-4064-8df0-4520538c0ef5", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 37, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 147, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P19\nLow Vision | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter could not read the text at the minimum zoom level and called a poll worker for help. The poll\nworker showed her how to increase the default zoom setting.\n2. The voter did not know how to write in a candidate and required additional instruction for a poll worker.\nThe participant had yet to see the write-in option during her voting session because she was at the\nmaximum zoom level and did not click the \"more\" button in order to scroll through additional candidates\nand possible write-In selections.\n3. Once the voter inserted the ballot into the scanner/tabulator, she had to call a poll worker in order to\nconfirm that she was finished voting.\n4. The voter needed confirmation from a poll worker that she had successfully cast his ballot.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625853+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ff28482e-6503-4272-8bf8-07371bf21313", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 38, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 30, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P20\nImpaired Mobility | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter needed confirmation from a poll worker that he had successfully cast his ballot.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625858+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "a3dcb7da-fdf9-490d-85aa-2a727c97a937", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 39, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 63, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P23\nImpaired mobility | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter struggled with initially inserting the ballot into the ExpressVote machine and eventually had to\ncall a poll worker for assistance.\n2. Once the voter inserted the ballot into the scanner/tabulator, she had to call a poll worker in order to\nconfirm that she was finished voting.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625863+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "777fd9ca-2515-4d82-8677-95de6cbde1da", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 40, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 39, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P24\nImpaired Mobility,\nImpaired Dexterity,\nand Hearing\nImpairment | INTERFACE\nUSED: Touch Screen | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter did not know how to write in a candidate and required additional instruction from a poll worker.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625868+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "14ee373c-f767-44f6-ba97-dd5235674f6d", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 41, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 42, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P26\nBlind and Over 65 | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter required a poll worker to escort him to the scanner, explain how to insert the ballot, and\nensure the process had been completed.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625873+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "77fb6d98-4dea-42b9-919e-c905f0c3f8be", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 42, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 64, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P27\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter did not know what a write-in was and needed it to be explained by the poll worker.\n2. The voter did not know how to insert a space into the name of her write-in candidate.\n3. The voter required a poll worker to escort her to the scanner.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625878+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "8fcc50d4-abe4-4965-87d6-eedbaa629cdf", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 43, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 39, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P28\nLow Vision | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter required a poll worker to escort her to the scanner.\n2. The voter needed confirmation that her vote had been successfully cast.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625883+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e51578a6-f586-4d52-8348-c27ef788e2ac", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting_system/documents/ExpressVote - Final Usability Report.pdf", "title": "ExpressVote   Final Usability Report", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting System", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 44, "chunk_total": 230, "word_count": 77, "text": "PARTICIPANT #: P29\nBlind | INTERFACE\nUSED: Navigation\nKeypad | SUMMARY OF ASSISTANCE: 1. The voter required a poll worker to escort him to the scanner.\n2. The scanner rejected the voter’s ballot and he required assistance from a poll worker. He was told to\ninsert the ballot into the upper slot of the scanner.\n3. After having correctly inserted the ballot into the scanner, the voter asked for confirmation that his vote\nhad been successfully cast.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:54.625889+00:00"}
