{"chunk_id": "9568fa42-f0c0-433e-ada6-fb382f8dfdea", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/coo.pdf", "title": "coo", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 27, "chunk_total": 28, "word_count": 10, "text": ": the voter. Date notice sent ____________ Staff Initials: ______________________", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:25.103676+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "50b1699a-bbde-46c4-bc79-e3866ecaa5f9", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/rocot.pdf", "title": "rocot", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 179, "text": "Officer Resignation Form\nIn accordance with §13-207(d)(1) of the Election Law Article, Annotated Code\nof Maryland, as of ___________________, __________ I hereby resign as:\n(month/day) (year)\nChairman for: ____________________________________________________________\n(Name of Campaign Finance Entity)\nTreasurer for: ____________________________________________________________\n(Name of Campaign Finance Entity)\nAnd, I hereby certify that I have returned all records relating to the campaign finance entity to\nthe remaining officer or the candidate and I have completed all of my campaign finance\nreporting responsibilities.*\n_______________________________________________________\nSignature of Resigning Officer\n_______________________________________________________\nPrinted Name of Resigning Officer\n_______________________\nDate\n*Depending on when you file your resignation, you may remain liable for the next Campaign Finance\nReport. Call the State Board of Elections to clarify your reporting responsibilities. In addition, it is\nrecommended that you file a statement with your resignation reporting your committee or entity’s cash\nbalance, the amount of money in the checking account, and any outstanding obligations.\nState Board of Elections\nDivision of Candidacy and Campaign Finance\n151 West Street, Suite 200/P.O. Box 6486, Annapolis, MD 21401-0486\n(410) 269-2880 (800) 222-8683 ext. 4\nSBE/CCF 13-207-1 Revised 03/2007", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:26.097342+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "2c6d2dcb-cfe8-4d8b-bda4-659b83a88da7", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/cfrsp.pdf", "title": "cfrsp", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 435, "text": "Maryland State Board of Elections\nCampaign Finance Report Summary Sheet\n\nPart 1\nEntity Name: Entity # Report Due Date:\nTransaction Period > This Report covers transactions beginning and ending\n\nDate Date\n\nQ) Final Report (Check if you intend to close the account. This cannot be a final report if a cash balance or outstanding obligation remains)\n8 Amendment # (Date amendment is being filed )\n\nPart 2\nBank Account Name Bank Account Number Bank Account Balance*\n\n*As of the report transaction ending date. Total |\n\nPart 3 Part 4\n\nReceipts\nContributions — Schd 1, Col A\n\nTicket Purchases — Schd 1, Col B\nFederal Committees — Schd 1, Col C Prior Balance\nPolitical Clubs — Schd 1, Col D\n\nMD Candidate and Slate Accounts — Schd 1A, Col E +\n\nReport calculated cash balance\nfrom Part 4 of your prior report.\n\nMD Party Central Committees — Schd 1A, Col F\nMD Political Action Committees — Schd 1A, Col G Total Receipts\nNon-Federal Out-of-State Committees — Schd 1A, Col H\nOther — Schd 1B, Col I -\n\nLoans — Schd 3, Col K .\nEnter Total in Part 4 (Total Receipts) Total Expenditures [ Total of Part 3 Expenditures\n\nTotal of Part 3 Receipts\n\nExpenditures _\n\nSalaries & Other Compensation — Schd 2, Col N ~\n\nRent & Other Office Expenses — Schd 2, Col O This is your report calculated cash\nField Expenses — Schd 2, Col P Cash Balance balance. Carry forward this\nMedia — Schd 2, Col Q balance to your next report.\n\nPrinting & Campaign Materials — Schd 2, Col R\nDirect Mailing by Mail House — Schd 2, Col S\n\nPostage — Schd 2, Col T Part 5\nPurchase of Equipment — Schd 2, Col U Value of In-Kind Contributions — Schd 1B, Col J\nFundraising Expenses — Schd 2, Col V Value of In-Kind Expenditures — Schd 2, Col AA\nTransfers Out — Schd 2, Col W\nLoan Repayment — Schd 2, Col X Part 6\nOther — Schd 2, Col Y Outstanding Loan Balance — Schd 3, Col L\nReturned Contribution — Schd 2, Col Z Outstanding Bills Due — Schd 3, Col M\nEnter Total in Part 4 (Total Expenditures) Total Outstanding Obligations\n\nPart 7\n\nUnder penalty of perjury, we declare that we have examined this report, including the accompanying schedules, and to the best of our\nknowledge and belief they are complete and accurate.\n\n(Date)\nSignature of Treasurer .\nWarning\n(Date) Failure to provide all information required by\nSignature of Chairman this form will be regarded as a failure to file.\n\nAll Reports must bear original signatures.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:28.519300+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "c72b1700-4fd3-4866-ad26-8c22b30d86fb", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s1.pdf", "title": "s1", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 209, "text": "Forms may be duplicated as needed Page ________ of ________\nReport Due Date _______________\nSchedule 1 – Contributions\n(see schedules 1A and 1B for other types of Income)\nSee instructions on reverse side\nName of Entity _______________________________________________________________________________\nEntity Number ___________________\nA B C D\nReceived From A Paid by Contributions Ticket Contributions Contributions\nD C C other than ticket purchases by from Federal from Political\nDate Name and Address of Contributor. M H A purchases from Individuals, Committees Clubs (include\nReceived I E S Individuals, Corporations (Include ticket ticket\nN C H Corporations, etc. purchases) purchases)\n(cid:1) K (cid:1) etc.\n(cid:1)\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nAggregate\nto Date:\nPrice Per\n$ Ticket: $\nTOTALS THIS PAGE A B C D\nFailure to provide all the information required by this form will be regarded as a FAILURE TO FILE.\nSBE-13-03 (Rev. 4/03)", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:29.635866+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "d054e3fb-9e2a-4c21-b6d5-465d1f220931", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s1a.pdf", "title": "s1a", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 157, "text": "Forms may be duplicated as needed. Page _______ of ________\nReport Due Date _______________\nSchedule 1A – Transfers in\n(see Schedules 1 and 1B for other types of Income)\nSee instructions on reverse side\nName of Entity _________________________________________________________________________\nEntity Number __________________________\nE F G H\nFrom MD From MD Party From MD PACs From Non-\nDate Name and Address of the Campaign Finance Entity from which the Candidate Central Federal Out of\nReceived Campaign Committees State PACs\ntransfer is received. Finance Entities\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nAggregate to\nDate\n$\nTOTALS THIS PAGE E F G H\nFailure to provide all the information required by this form will be regarded as a FAILURE TO FILE.\nSBE-13-03 (Rev.4/03)", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:30.626796+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "89b3070b-2207-40d9-b2ba-d470e5447c87", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s1b.pdf", "title": "s1b", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 134, "text": "Page ____ of _______\nReport Due Date _______________\nSchedule 1B\nOther Receipts and In-Kind Contributions\n(see Schedules 1 and 1A for other types of Income)\nSee instructions on reverse side\nName of Entity __________________________________________________________________________\nEntity Number _________________\nI J\nDate Complete Name and Address of Payor Other - Refunds, In-Kind Contribution - A Remarks\nReceived Rebates, Items sold, Fair Market Value of D\ninterest or misc. In-Kind Contribution M\nI\nincome. (Describe in Received. (Describe in\nN\nRemarks) Remarks)\n(cid:1)\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nAggregate to Date:\n$\nTotals This Page\nI J\nFailure to provide all the information required by this form will be regarded as a FAILURE TO FILE.\nSBE-13-03 (Rev. 4-03)", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:31.713952+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "91677d5b-acda-42be-8d41-8cb6036a206b", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s2.pdf", "title": "s2", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 2, "word_count": 70, "text": "Code: Description | N: Salaries and\nother\ncompensation | O: Rent and\nother office\nexpenses | P*: Field\nExpenses | Q: Media | R: Printing and\nCampaign\nMaterials | S: Direct\nMailing by\nMail House | T: Postage | U*: Purchase of\nEquipment | V*: Fundraising\nExpenses | W: Transfers\nOut to Other\nMaryland\nTreasurers | X: Loan\nRepayment | Y*: Other | Z: Returned\nContribution | AA*: In-kind\nExpenditure", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:32.873449+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "d2e5f68b-cbd4-4af3-a28b-9a90785f7621", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s2.pdf", "title": "s2", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 2, "word_count": 2, "text": "Code: Totals", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:32.873466+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ec16a331-2b6f-4956-9369-6e71c56e67a3", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s3.pdf", "title": "s3", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 120, "text": "Page ________ of ________\nReport Due Date _______________\nSchedule 3 – Outstanding Obligations\nSee instructions on reverse side\nName of Entity _____________________________________________________________________________________________\nEntity Number _________________\nLoans Unpaid Bills Other Than Loans\nK L M\nName and Address of Creditor Date Loan If this is a new Written Consent Prime Rate on Interest Rate Charged Balance Due Balance Due Description\nAccepted or loan, state the filed herewith. Day Loan is (if less than prime rate,\nobligation total amount of (yes or no) Accepted indicate in-kind interest\nincurred the loan. contribution on Schedule\n1B)\nTotals This Page\nK L M\nFailure to provide all of the information required by this form will be regarded as a FAILURE TO FILE.\nSBE-13-03 (Rev. 4/03)", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:33.869083+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "99b0c370-9a64-4a45-bed0-479180912a81", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/s4.pdf", "title": "s4", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 290, "text": "Schedule 4 – Loan Consent Form1\nTerms of Loan\nAmount of Loan _________________________________________________________\nSchedule for Repayment2 __________________________________________________\nInterest Charged3 ___________ Prime Rate on the Day Loan is Made4 ____________\nLender Information\nName of Lender ________________________________________________________\nAddress of Lender ______________________________________________________\nSignature of Lender _____________________________________________________\nDate\nRecipient Information\nName of Campaign Finance Entity ___________________________________________\nEntity Number\nName of Treasurer _______________________________________________________\nSignature of Treasurer5 ____________________________________________________\nDate\nConsent of Candidate\nI, ______________________________, hereby acknowledge receipt on ____________________\nName of Candidate Date\nof a loan in the amount of $_________ from __________________________________________\nName of Lender\nto ____________________________________________________________________________\nName of Campaign Finance Entity\nA copy of this consent has been supplied to the lender.\n_______________________________________________________________\nSignature of Candidate Date\n1 The loan consent form is not required to be filed if the loan is from the candidate or the candidate’s spouse to the\ncandidate’s own campaign committee and if interest is not being charged on the loan.\n2 Loans must be repaid by the end of the next election cycle. If full repayment is not made, the balance due will be\nconsidered a contribution, unless the loan is from a financial institution in the business of making loans.\n3 If the interest rate charged is less than the prime rate, the difference constitutes an in-kind contribution which must be\nreported on Schedule 1B of the current report.\n4 Enter the bank lending prime rate on the day the loan was made. The prime rate can be ascertained by calling your\nlocal bank or contacting the State Board of Elections.\n5 A non-candidate committee must provide the signature of the treasurer to acknowledge receipt of the loan. Candidate\ncommittees only need to have the candidate fill out and sign the Consent of Candidate box.\nSBE-13-03 (Rev. 4/03)", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:34.914869+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "26542ab9-691d-4d8f-970d-257bdf4e7ddc", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/aodf.pdf", "title": "aodf", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 163, "text": "Campaign Finance Report\nAmendment Description Form\nMaryland State Board of Elections\nDivision of Candidacy and Campaign Finance\nP.O. Box 6486 (cid:127) 151 West Street, Suite 200 (cid:127) Annapolis, MD 21401-0486\n410- 269-2880 (cid:127) 800- 222-8683 (cid:127) MD Relay 800-735-2258\nName of Campaign Finance Entity ___________________________________________\nEntity # ____________\nDue Date of Report Being Amended _______________\nForms being amended Page # Describe Change (what is being changed and why)\n(cid:1) Summary Sheet\n(cid:1) Schedule 1\n(cid:1) Schedule 1A\n(cid:1) Schedule 1B\n(cid:1) Schedule 2\n(cid:1) Schedule 3\n(cid:1) Schedule 4\n_________________________________________________________________\nSignature of Treasurer (required for all entities) Date\n_________________________________________________________________\nSignature of Chairman (required for committees or slates) Date\n_________________________________________________________________\nSignature of Candidate (required if the entity is a personal treasurer) Date\nImportant. This form should not be used by a campaign finance entity that files its Campaign\nFinance Reports using ELECTrack (the State’s free filing software). ELECTrack automatically\ngenerates an Amendment Description form that should be filed instead of this form.\nRevised 4/03", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:36.173045+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "448e9a74-8f71-46f9-a265-7f1606104ce9", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/sd.pdf", "title": "sd", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 153, "text": "Slate Designation/Resignation Form\nName of Slate: ________________________________________________________________\nSlate Chairman: ____________________ Slate Treasurer: __________________________\nCandidate Information\nName of Candidate\nResidence Address\nCounty of Residence\n(or Baltimore City)\nParty Affiliation\nIn accordance with § 13-209 of the Election Law Article, Annotated Code of Maryland I\nhereby certify that it is my intention to join the above referenced Slate.\n____________________________________________________________\nSignature of Candidate Date\nI wish to resign my previously filed designation to the above referenced Slate.\n____________________________________________________________\nSignature of Candidate Date\nThis form should be sent to the State Board of Elections or a local election office, depending\nupon where the Slate is filed.\nFor Board Use Only\nSl ate Entity Number: ____________________\nCandidate Entity Number: _______________\nMaryland State Board of Elections\nDivision of Candidacy and Campaign Finance\nP.O. Box 6486 (cid:122) 151 West Street, Suite 200 (cid:122) Annapolis, MD 21401-0486\n410-269-2880 (cid:122) 800-222-8683 (cid:122) MD Relay 800-735-2258\nwww.elections.state.md.us\nSBE/CCF Form # 13-209 Revised 08/2007", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:37.406963+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "093ab748-a2c6-4362-98c2-7c5d78dc792e", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/Request_for_Accessible_Polling_Place.pdf", "title": "Request for Accessible Polling Place", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 450, "text": "Please complete this form and mail or deliver it to your Board of Elections at least 21 days before the first election for which it is to\nbe effective. The Board of Elections will do its best to accommodate your request, but if it is not possible to assign you to an\naccessible or another polling place, the board will notify you and issue you an absentee ballot.\nPart 1: Voter Information\nName: Date of Birth:\nResidence Address:\nNumber and Street City Zip\nMailing Address for Absentee Ballot (if different):\nNumber and Street City State Zip\nSignature Date Telephone Number\nPart 2: Reason for Requesting a New Polling Place\nPlease check the box that explains why you are asking for a new polling place or an absentee ballot. I am a registered voter and:\n□\nI am 65 years of age or older and/or have a disability, and my assigned polling place is not structurally barrier free or accessible\nto me.\n□ □\nI would like to be reassigned to an accessible polling OR I would like an absentee ballot for:\n□\nplace: April 2020 Presidential Primary Election\n□ □\nUntil I provide further notice to the election office; or November 2020 Presidential General Election\n□\nFor the following elections:\n□\nApril 2020 Presidential Primary Election\n□\nNovember 2020 Presidential General Election\n□\nI would like my polling place changed because I am the spouse or helper of an elderly voter or a voter with a disability. I am\nregistered to vote in the same county as this voter and wish to be reassigned to the same polling place. I understand that I will\nonly be reassigned if this voter’s polling place will have my ballot available.\nPrinted Name of Elderly Voter or Voter with a Disability:\n□\nI would like my polling place changed because entering my polling place conflicts with my bona fide religious beliefs and\npractices.\nPart 3: Assistance with Form\nDid someone help you complete this form?\n□\nYes\n□\nNo\nIf yes, the individual who helped you must read and complete the following: Under penalty of perjury, I hereby certify that the\nvoter named above, who requires assistance because of disability or inability to read or write, authorized me to complete this\nform for him or her. If the voter was unable to sign this form, I have printed the voter’s name, followed by my initials.\nSignature of Assistant: Date:\nPrinted Name of Assistant:\n□ □\nFor Board of Elections Use Only: Approved Not approved - reason/date: ______________________________________________________\n□\nComment/Action: _______________ Voter reassigned to: _______________________________ Voter provided Absentee Ballot\nDate voter notified: ________________ Signature of Board Official:______________________________________________________________________\nSBE-10-102-2-Rev. 12/2018 L:\\Library\\Elections\\Polling_Place\\Request for Accessible Polling Place Form", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:38.763593+00:00"}
